    "risk_summary": "Target is not universally superior: ZrTc2 and several ternary children have larger source responses; Lu increases lambda but lowers Tc. Tc radioactivity limits practical follow-up, not this computation. Scalar NC treatment and C14 competitor are explicit. Zero SCF forces and positive sampled phonon evidence support a near-zero-pressure local source minimum, not bulk ground-state synthesis. Saved q2 all12 representations converge, all18 nonzero-q frequencies positive, and ten Ry Gaussian widths contain all18 lambda/gamma modes. No native exit inferred. C14 competition, SOC, radioactivity and metaphase retention remain bounded risks.",
    "ambient_scope": "Source coarse force 0.0 eV/Å, pressure -0.002 GPa; fine force 0.0 eV/Å, pressure -0.22999999999999998 GPa. Actual full stress, Γ interval, finite path and q observations are retained in the complete review; no whole-BZ/global-stability claim.",
    "route_response": "Re-to-Tc replacement in the C15 HfX2 network. coupled chemical/site-role/volume/mass construction, not isolated geometry or inferred W/n",
    "next_action": "Compare the existing C15 branch with published C14 phase and source-controlled Re→Tc EPC. Favorable: C15 retains local stability and pairing advantage as a viable metastable branch; adverse: exact-known C15 alias or phase competition removes distinct useful state; ambiguous: phase-level literature cannot settle exact association.",
